1
00:00:07,913 --> 00:00:13,182
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,421 --> 00:00:15,429
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:19,658 --> 00:00:21,043
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

4
00:00:21,068 --> 00:00:21,955
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

5
00:00:22,754 --> 00:00:26,644
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

6
00:00:27,298 --> 00:00:29,134
السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاتهَ

7
00:00:30,254 --> 00:00:36,629
Rasool Allah ﷺ tried to break the coalition that was part of his strategy.

8
00:00:37,089 --> 00:00:38,010
 So what he did?

9
00:00:38,335 --> 00:00:42,272
He tried to negotiate a deal with Ghatafaan(غطفان),

10
00:00:43,074 --> 00:00:45,467
Ghatafaan(غطفان) are these tribes from Najd(نجد),

11
00:00:45,507 --> 00:00:49,511
who came and participated in the coalition with the force of 6000.

12
00:00:49,551 --> 00:00:56,523
Now the entire coalition was 10,000, so they are more than half of the entire coalition.

13
00:00:56,959 --> 00:00:59,189
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was trying to work a deal with them.

14
00:00:59,553 --> 00:01:03,164
Rasool Allah ﷺ met with their two leaders

15
00:01:04,056 --> 00:01:08,556
and he proposed to them that they withdraw from coalition

16
00:01:09,338 --> 00:01:14,399
in exchange Rasool Allah ﷺ is gonna pay them one third of the harvest of Madina.

17
00:01:15,425 --> 00:01:18,368
They agreed and they wrote up a document

18
00:01:19,124 --> 00:01:22,696
but they did not finalize it by bringing the witnesses.

19
00:01:23,823 --> 00:01:29,671
Rasool Allah ﷺ calls Sa'ad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ) and Sa'ad Bin Ubadah(سعد بن عبادة) who are the heads of Al-Ansaar(الانصار)

20
00:01:30,202 --> 00:01:31,329
and he make Shura(شورى) with them.

21
00:01:31,369 --> 00:01:34,111
 And notice here that Rasool Allah ﷺ only made Shura(شورى) with them

22
00:01:34,710 --> 00:01:37,041
and this shows you that Shura(شورى) is not done with everyone,

23
00:01:37,149 --> 00:01:41,150
Shura(شورى) is done with the pertaining people to every situation.

24
00:01:42,336 --> 00:01:46,049
Now since, Rasool Allah ﷺ is here offering one third of the harvest of Madina

25
00:01:46,444 --> 00:01:48,081
which belongs to Al-Aos(الأوس) Wal Khazraj(ولخزرج).

26
00:01:48,152 --> 00:01:50,462
 He needs to seek their counsel.

27
00:01:51,437 --> 00:01:54,580
So, he told them, what he proposed to Ghatafaan(غطفان),

28
00:01:55,310 --> 00:01:56,649
they responded by saying;

29
00:01:56,983 --> 00:02:00,380
Messenger of Allah, is this something that you wish to do

30
00:02:01,110 --> 00:02:04,516
something Allah has ordered you to do and which we must put into effect?

31
00:02:04,596 --> 00:02:06,961
 Or is it something you are doing for our sake?

32
00:02:08,393 --> 00:02:10,583
If it is something from Allahعَزّوجَلّ, we will accept it,

33
00:02:10,623 --> 00:02:14,277
but if it's your opinion and you're doing it for our sake, let us know.

34
00:02:14,651 --> 00:02:16,833
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, Yes, I'm doing it, for your sake.

35
00:02:18,024 --> 00:02:19,327
Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) said;

36
00:02:20,287 --> 00:02:24,200
Messenger of Allah, We used to be disbelievers in Allah

37
00:02:24,287 --> 00:02:29,067
and worshiped idols along with those people, not worshipping nor knowing Allah.

38
00:02:29,810 --> 00:02:34,429
At that time they would never have dreamed of eating a single date of ours

39
00:02:34,469 --> 00:02:36,993
except as our guests or after purchase.

40
00:02:38,729 --> 00:02:40,721
Should we give them our property now,

41
00:02:41,086 --> 00:02:47,127
after Allah has honored us with Islam led us to Him and given us esteem through you and through Him.

42
00:02:47,752 --> 00:02:50,860
We will have none of this, by Allah.

43
00:02:51,321 --> 00:02:55,878
All we will give them is the sword, until Allah decides between us and them.

44
00:02:57,206 --> 00:02:59,741
Sa'ad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ) and Sa'ad Bin Ubadah(سعد بن عبادة) are saying;

45
00:03:00,081 --> 00:03:04,079
These people would not have dreamed of getting one date of us

46
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:09,209
except if they would pay the price for it or if we give it to them as our guests

47
00:03:09,751 --> 00:03:13,177
and now we're just going to give it to them, for free so that they leave.

48
00:03:13,721 --> 00:03:15,645
We don't want to have anything to do with this.

49
00:03:16,558 --> 00:03:18,486
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; As you wish.

50
00:03:18,806 --> 00:03:22,247
So, Sa'ad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ) took the document from Rasool Allah ﷺ

51
00:03:22,674 --> 00:03:24,856
and he erased the writing from it saying;

52
00:03:25,078 --> 00:03:28,178
Now let them fight us, Now let them fight us.

53
00:03:29,955 --> 00:03:31,815
So, brothers and sisters,

54
00:03:32,228 --> 00:03:35,974
Again, you can see the Ansaar(انصار) and how they would approach matters.

55
00:03:36,014 --> 00:03:39,357
Rasool Allah ﷺ was willing to negotiate this matter,

56
00:03:39,397 --> 00:03:42,897
but the Ansaar(انصار) said; No, We're gonna fight, let's just fight.

57
00:03:43,857 --> 00:03:47,351
 May Allahعَزّوجَلّ has His mercies on them.

58
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:51,430
So, this is the issue with Ghatafaan(غطفان).

59
00:03:51,470 --> 00:03:54,097
Obviously the whole thing didn't go through.

60
00:03:54,829 --> 00:04:04,317
Now because the Muslims, through their Eeman(ايمان), qualified in the eyes of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, for victory

61
00:04:04,706 --> 00:04:05,960
Allah was going to help them.

62
00:04:07,365 --> 00:04:11,782
You know, you could be in a disadvantage compared to your enemy.

63
00:04:12,511 --> 00:04:15,963
And from every angle you look at it, there's no way you can win.

64
00:04:17,495 --> 00:04:25,003
But because you deserve to win, since you have fulfilled the requirements of winning in the eyes of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

65
00:04:25,225 --> 00:04:27,154
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is gonna find a way out for you.

66
00:04:27,368 --> 00:04:30,659
وَمَنْ يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَلْ لَهُ مَخْرَجًا۝وَيَرْزُقْهُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَحْتَسِبُ ۚ

67
00:04:31,122 --> 00:04:32,725
If you have Taqwa(تقوى) in Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

68
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:37,893
Allah will find the way out for you and will provide you from avenues, you never expected.

69
00:04:38,426 --> 00:04:40,629
So, underline here the word you never expected.

70
00:04:40,701 --> 00:04:44,889
I mean it's going to come from a place, a quarter that you didn't expect.

71
00:04:45,329 --> 00:04:48,709
You looked at all of the various variables, you assess the situation.

72
00:04:48,907 --> 00:04:50,156
There's no way you can make it.

73
00:04:51,325 --> 00:04:53,583
But Allahعَزّوجَلّ knows, what you don't know.

74
00:04:54,979 --> 00:04:58,835
A man came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, his name is Nuaim Bin Masood(نُعَيْم بن مسعود).

75
00:04:59,905 --> 00:05:01,551
This man is from Ghatafaan(غطفان).

76
00:05:02,575 --> 00:05:04,676
He comes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and says;

77
00:05:05,214 --> 00:05:11,415
Messenger of Allah, I have accepted Islam, but my people do not know of this.

78
00:05:12,166 --> 00:05:14,603
Give me whatever orders, you wish.

79
00:05:15,897 --> 00:05:19,225
Here this man comes out of nowhere and says I'm a Muslim

80
00:05:19,990 --> 00:05:24,154
and Subhan Allah(سبحان الله) it appears to be the wrong time to become a Muslim.

81
00:05:24,189 --> 00:05:26,145
I mean the Muslims are under siege.

82
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:30,669
It appears that they are losing and you want to become Muslim.

83
00:05:31,014 --> 00:05:33,115
Well that's because, he was a soldier of Allah.

84
00:05:34,139 --> 00:05:38,684
Allah was bringing this man forward because he was one of the soldiers of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

85
00:05:39,503 --> 00:05:41,512
وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُودَ رَبِّكَ إِلَّا هُوَ ۚ

86
00:05:41,552 --> 00:05:44,399
Only Allah knows His soldiers, we don't know them.

87
00:05:44,671 --> 00:05:48,302
So, he comes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and says; "Order me, Give me your orders."

88
00:05:48,942 --> 00:05:50,250
The Messenger of Allah said;

89
00:05:50,626 --> 00:05:58,304
You are only one man, use trickery to relieve us, of them, if you can, War is deception.

90
00:05:59,166 --> 00:06:02,227
Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling Nuaim(نُعَيْم) that if you join us

91
00:06:02,943 --> 00:06:06,472
 we're going to be 3001, it doesn't really make a difference, you're just one man.

92
00:06:07,291 --> 00:06:10,613
But since they do not know that you have become Muslim,

93
00:06:10,931 --> 00:06:17,362
go back, go back and try to weaken them, because war is deception.

94
00:06:17,592 --> 00:06:21,408
In other words, Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying that you can use deception

95
00:06:21,998 --> 00:06:27,485
if that will support the cause of relieving us, of them.

96
00:06:28,567 --> 00:06:35,315
Nuaim رضي الله عنه left and he went to the Jews of Bannu Quraidha(بنو قريظه).

97
00:06:35,561 --> 00:06:42,859
Now the thing here with Nuaim(نُعَيْم), he had good relations with the Jews, good relations with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

98
00:06:43,226 --> 00:06:46,219
And since he was from Ghatafaan(غطفان), he had good relations with his people.

99
00:06:46,889 --> 00:06:52,528
Nuaim Bin Masood رضي الله عنه was a well known man, a trusted man.

100
00:06:53,050 --> 00:06:55,188
So he went to Bannu Quraidha(بنو قريظه) and he told them;

101
00:06:55,571 --> 00:07:00,705
You know me and I know you and you know our friendship

102
00:07:01,707 --> 00:07:05,259
and you know that I would only give you a sincere advice.

103
00:07:06,039 --> 00:07:08,066
What you have done is wrong.

104
00:07:09,103 --> 00:07:12,531
You have decided to fight against Muhammadﷺ,

105
00:07:12,885 --> 00:07:17,658
but you are living in Madina, your women and children and property are here,

106
00:07:18,748 --> 00:07:23,214
while Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and Ghatafaan(غطفان) are coming over to fight

107
00:07:23,323 --> 00:07:26,419
 but their women children and property or somewhere else.

108
00:07:27,333 --> 00:07:33,094
Now Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and Ghatafaan(غطفان) are going to try to seize the opportunity to defeat Muhammadﷺ

109
00:07:33,134 --> 00:07:37,700
but if that opportunity doesn't arise they're going to pack up and leave.

110
00:07:38,414 --> 00:07:40,694
 And you know what will happen if they leave

111
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:46,370
Muhammadﷺ will attack you first, since you are right there with him, in Madina,

112
00:07:46,830 --> 00:07:52,779
and you know that you cannot face off alone against Muhammadﷺ.

113
00:07:53,421 --> 00:07:56,077
They said, Well, what you saying is true. What shall we do?

114
00:07:56,613 --> 00:07:57,078
He said;

115
00:07:57,215 --> 00:08:04,101
You want to make sure that Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and Ghatafaan(غطفان), are willing to fight until the end

116
00:08:04,569 --> 00:08:09,574
until you achieve the objective, not just try to win, if it doesn't work out, then they leave.

117
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:10,261
 No.

118
00:08:10,394 --> 00:08:16,108
you want to make sure that they will stay behind and fight with you and not betray you and leave.

119
00:08:17,125 --> 00:08:20,533
 They said, All right, well tell us how we can guarantee that.

120
00:08:20,924 --> 00:08:27,910
He said; Ask them to leave some of their men with you, as assurance

121
00:08:28,281 --> 00:08:30,438
meaning you take some of their men as hostages.

122
00:08:31,487 --> 00:08:33,613
And this was a practice that existed in those days.

123
00:08:33,653 --> 00:08:38,242
 I mean you could borrow money, and then you could leave your child as a security.

124
00:08:38,655 --> 00:08:42,197
So I mean, it wasn't something that was strange, it did exist in those days.

125
00:08:42,861 --> 00:08:43,960
So Nuaim(نُعَيْم) here is saying;

126
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:49,421
Ask them to hand over some of their men both from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and from Ghatafaan(غَطَفَان)

127
00:08:49,652 --> 00:08:54,882
and hold them with you as an assurance, as a guarantee that they're going to fight until the end.

128
00:08:55,578 --> 00:08:56,859
They said; That's a good idea.

129
00:08:57,148 --> 00:08:58,519
We agree, we'll do that.

130
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:03,548
Now Nuaim(نُعَيْم) leaves the Jews and he goes to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and he tells them

131
00:09:03,847 --> 00:09:06,753
you know, how close our friendship is

132
00:09:07,179 --> 00:09:12,942
and you understand, that I would be sincere in my advice to you.

133
00:09:13,447 --> 00:09:15,943
And I would only tell you the truth

134
00:09:16,723 --> 00:09:19,781
and I've come here because I have something to disclose to you

135
00:09:19,865 --> 00:09:22,887
and I want you to keep this information classified.

136
00:09:23,734 --> 00:09:26,410
They said, Yes, Nuaim(نُعَيْم) we trust you and we know that.

137
00:09:26,835 --> 00:09:27,538
Go ahead.

138
00:09:27,773 --> 00:09:28,466
He said;

139
00:09:28,671 --> 00:09:37,086
The Jews have regretted the fact that they have abrogated their agreement with Muhammadﷺ

140
00:09:37,629 --> 00:09:44,085
and now they are involved in negotiations with him to bring back the agreement.

141
00:09:44,733 --> 00:09:46,684
And they have offered Muhammad(محمد)

142
00:09:46,914 --> 00:09:53,395
to handover some of your men to him to be executed

143
00:09:53,806 --> 00:09:59,037
as a sign of their sincerity and repentance of their deed.

144
00:09:59,741 --> 00:10:07,260
So, Nuaim(نُعَيْم) is here telling Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) that the Jews are sorry that they have broken their agreement with Muhammadﷺ

145
00:10:07,821 --> 00:10:13,367
and they are willing to make that up by handing over some of your men, to him.

146
00:10:14,139 --> 00:10:20,163
So if the Jews come to you asking for hostages do not give them any.

147
00:10:20,504 --> 00:10:23,750
And then he goes to the Ghatafaan(غطفان) and tells them the exact same thing.

148
00:10:24,212 --> 00:10:30,145
 Now, the siege was taking a long time and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are getting fed up

149
00:10:30,225 --> 00:10:34,352
 now remember Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) didn't come to Madina to lay siege to it.

150
00:10:34,821 --> 00:10:41,087
 They came in to fight and they were surprised to find this moat in front of them, the trench.

151
00:10:41,577 --> 00:10:45,144
So, they did not come in with supplies to last for a siege.

152
00:10:45,238 --> 00:10:48,895
They came in for a fast battle, get it over with and leave.

153
00:10:49,097 --> 00:10:51,476
So, they weren't prepared to wait for a long time.

154
00:10:52,247 --> 00:10:58,656
So, Ikrimah Bin Abi Jahal(عكرمه بن ابي جهل) was sent to head the delegation to go and meet with the Jews of Bannu Quraidha(بنو قريظه).

155
00:10:59,140 --> 00:11:00,378
 He went to them and said;

156
00:11:00,690 --> 00:11:04,772
That we're getting tired of this long siege, our camels and horses are dying

157
00:11:05,613 --> 00:11:10,179
and we want to wage an all out war on Muhammad(محمد), so get yourselves ready

158
00:11:10,626 --> 00:11:12,416
and we shall attack today.

159
00:11:13,049 --> 00:11:16,632
The Jews said, No, you know that we don't fight in the Sabbath(السابت).

160
00:11:17,006 --> 00:11:20,900
And some of our people, who did fight in the Sabbath(السابت), this and this happened to them.

161
00:11:21,519 --> 00:11:26,370
They went on talking about the history of staying away from fighting on the Sabbath(السابت).

162
00:11:26,414 --> 00:11:28,010
 And then they said, Plus

163
00:11:28,528 --> 00:11:32,429
you know, we're worried that you might not stay the course

164
00:11:32,815 --> 00:11:36,841
and to ensure that you are willing to fight until the end

165
00:11:37,172 --> 00:11:41,376
we want you to hand over some of your men as a guarantee.

166
00:11:42,203 --> 00:11:45,362
Iqrimah(عكرمه) goes back and conveys this information to Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان),

167
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:50,276
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) said, this is it, this is what Nuaim(نُعَيْم) told us

168
00:11:51,037 --> 00:11:56,182
that the Jews have betrayed us and they want to hand over, our men to Muhammadﷺ.

169
00:11:56,769 --> 00:11:59,772
So, Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) answers back and said;

170
00:12:00,035 --> 00:12:04,141
We're not going to hand over even one man, not one single person.

171
00:12:04,684 --> 00:12:07,455
The jews said, this is exactly, what Nuaim(نُعَيْم) told us.

172
00:12:07,574 --> 00:12:13,779
These men are not serious and they're going to leave us alone to suffer the attacks of Muhammadﷺ.

173
00:12:14,551 --> 00:12:16,844
And the same thing happened with Ghatafaan(غطفان).

174
00:12:17,329 --> 00:12:25,036
And therefore one single man was successful in breaking up this coalition.

175
00:12:26,012 --> 00:12:29,746
The coalition that was brought together by the Yahood(يهود)

176
00:12:30,515 --> 00:12:38,063
headed by Huyaiye Bin Akhtab(حيئي بن اخطب) was now broken through one of many soldiers of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

177
00:12:38,532 --> 00:12:39,112
And as I said

178
00:12:39,152 --> 00:12:44,994
this help, it appears as if it came out of nowhere, but it was part of the Qadar(قدر) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

179
00:12:45,246 --> 00:12:47,277
because the Muslims have passed the test.

180
00:12:48,056 --> 00:12:55,590
The Muslims have passed the test of Eeman(ايمان) of perseverance, of endurance, patience, trust in Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

181
00:12:55,939 --> 00:12:58,240
Since they are past all of these requirements.

182
00:12:58,543 --> 00:13:00,621
Now Allah(عَزّوجَلّ) is going to find a way out for them.

183
00:13:01,958 --> 00:13:06,997
Just like when Musa(موسى) and Bannu Israel(بنواسرائيل) were faced with the sea in front of them and Firoun(فرعون) from behind them

184
00:13:07,152 --> 00:13:10,342
it was a test for them, to see, if they believe in the promise of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

185
00:13:10,418 --> 00:13:12,645
that He will save them and protect them or not

186
00:13:12,917 --> 00:13:15,015
many of them failed, some of them did pass.

187
00:13:15,583 --> 00:13:19,320
And that is when after the test was over Allahعَزّوجَلّ told Musa(موسى)

188
00:13:19,378 --> 00:13:22,964
all what you have to do is strike the sea with your stick and it'll split.

189
00:13:23,563 --> 00:13:25,057
 So, the whole thing was a test.

190
00:13:25,781 --> 00:13:30,348
Nuaim Bin Masood(نٌعَيْم بن مسعود) single handedly brought an end to this coalition.

191
00:13:30,965 --> 00:13:36,016
Let's talk about some lessons from these two incidents

192
00:13:36,073 --> 00:13:38,266
the one with Ghatafaan(غتفان) and the one with Nuaim Bin Masood(نٌعَيْم بن مسعود).

193
00:13:39,077 --> 00:13:43,174
Rasool Allah ﷺ made or negotiated with Ghatafaan(غطفان)

194
00:13:44,137 --> 00:13:47,908
because they were there only for financial gain.

195
00:13:48,527 --> 00:13:51,250
But the Jews and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were fighting a war of Aqeedah(عقيده),

196
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:55,406
their objective was to bring down Islam from its foundations

197
00:13:55,965 --> 00:13:58,705
and therefore, he didn't even attempt to negotiate with them.

198
00:13:59,106 --> 00:14:03,636
So, you need to know the objectives of your enemy.

199
00:14:04,398 --> 00:14:07,219
Is the enemy fighting because of Aqeedah(عقيده)?

200
00:14:07,544 --> 00:14:10,365
Or the enemy is fighting for another reason?

201
00:14:10,765 --> 00:14:12,580
Or is it the combination of both?

202
00:14:13,128 --> 00:14:16,527
See with Ghatafaan(غطفان), they were drawn into this because they're going to make money.

203
00:14:17,021 --> 00:14:21,495
And if they can make money off Muhammadﷺ then be it, we'll leave And they agreed.

204
00:14:22,117 --> 00:14:27,136
But Rasool Allah ﷺ never attempted to do that with the Jews or with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

205
00:14:27,371 --> 00:14:31,135
because they were fighting from a standpoint of Aqeedah(عقيده).

206
00:14:31,664 --> 00:14:33,980
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were fighting to defend their religion

207
00:14:34,662 --> 00:14:38,388
and to take revenge of those men from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), who became Muslim

208
00:14:38,773 --> 00:14:41,918
and the Jews were also fighting from Aqeedah(عقيده) point of view.

209
00:14:42,801 --> 00:14:46,989
So, it's important to know, to try to study the enemy.

210
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:48,340
Second lesson,

211
00:14:48,930 --> 00:14:52,707
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Sa'ad Bin Ubadah(سعد بن عبادة) and Sa'ad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ),

212
00:14:52,747 --> 00:14:56,209
 that the reason why he was making this offer is because

213
00:14:56,249 --> 00:15:03,200
he saw that the Arabs are, as if they are shooting you, from one single bow.

214
00:15:03,663 --> 00:15:08,026
Meaning that they have unified against you and I want to break up that coalition.

215
00:15:08,178 --> 00:15:11,522
اِنِيْ رَاَيْتُ الْعَرَبَ رَمَتْكُمْ عنْ قَوْسٍ وَاحِدَة

216
00:15:12,055 --> 00:15:17,061
So, the lesson here is that the Muslim leader needs to have Hikmah(حكمه)

217
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:25,090
and if it's possible to neutralize a particular party, and some of the enemies of Islam

218
00:15:25,867 --> 00:15:30,840
rather than have them all face at once, that can be part of the strategy.

219
00:15:31,458 --> 00:15:35,166
And the Muslims should not try to make enemies

220
00:15:35,773 --> 00:15:41,498
but they should try to neutralize the enemy, as long as this is done without giving up some of our principles.

221
00:15:42,624 --> 00:15:44,933
Why fight everybody at once?

222
00:15:45,281 --> 00:15:47,812
That was where Rasool Allah ﷺ was coming from.

223
00:15:48,050 --> 00:15:53,288
He was trying to break up this coalition Ghatafaan(غطفان), we can deal with them later.

224
00:15:53,649 --> 00:15:57,558
Let's deal with the priority now which is Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and Al-Yahood(اليهود).

225
00:15:58,020 --> 00:16:01,746
 Now one can argue that this was before the ruling of Allah

226
00:16:01,802 --> 00:16:02,911
وَقَاتِلُوا الْمُشْرِكِينَ كَافَّةً

227
00:16:03,064 --> 00:16:04,923
Now fight all of the disbelievers.

228
00:16:05,262 --> 00:16:09,011
But even then, if the Muslims do not have the capability of doing that

229
00:16:09,414 --> 00:16:16,228
they can strategize and ranked them according to how dangerous they are as enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

230
00:16:17,238 --> 00:16:25,959
 Next lesson, the leader should have the capability of taking advantage of the abilities of his soldiers.

231
00:16:26,413 --> 00:16:34,492
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ here didn't invite Nuaim(نُعَيْم) to come over and just give him a sword, and give him a spear and tell him well go and fight.

232
00:16:34,927 --> 00:16:39,795
No, Rasool Allah ﷺ knew where to use Nuaim Bin Masood(نُعَيْمْ بن مسعود).

233
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:43,403
 So, the leader needs to know, the qualities of his followers

234
00:16:43,690 --> 00:16:46,126
and put each person in the right place.

235
00:16:46,937 --> 00:16:49,605
Put the right person in the right place, to do the right thing.

236
00:16:51,157 --> 00:16:56,676
Rasool Allah ﷺ was using a powerful weapon against the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ and that is Dua(دعا).

237
00:16:57,661 --> 00:16:58,773
Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying,

238
00:16:58,813 --> 00:17:00,815
O Allah, revealer of the book,

239
00:17:01,392 --> 00:17:02,694
 quick to take account

240
00:17:03,102 --> 00:17:04,532
defeat the clans,

241
00:17:04,928 --> 00:17:07,349
 O Allah defeat them, and shake them.

242
00:17:07,824 --> 00:17:13,304
Allahعَزّوجَلّ accepted the Dua(دعا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and He assisted the Muslims with soldiers, they did not see.

243
00:17:13,628 --> 00:17:14,723
 Allahعَزّوجَلّ says,

244
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:29,468
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَةَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذْ جَاءَتْكُمْ جُنُودٌ فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِيحًا

245
00:17:30,056 --> 00:17:40,382
فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِيحًا وَجُنُودًا لَمْ تَرَوْهَا ۚ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرًا۝

246
00:17:42,113 --> 00:17:47,089
O you, who have believed, remember the favor of Allah upon you,

247
00:17:47,801 --> 00:17:54,328
when armies came to attack you and we sent upon them a wind and armies you did not see.

248
00:17:54,825 --> 00:17:57,675
Allah sent armies that they did not see, the Malaikah(ملائكه)

249
00:17:58,385 --> 00:18:01,986
wind were all armies sent by Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

250
00:18:02,026 --> 00:18:05,290
And we'll talk about wind, later on in the story of Hudaifah(حذيفة).

251
00:18:05,679 --> 00:18:09,193
And ever is Allah of what you do, seeing.

252
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:15,067
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is now sending soldiers from His armies, to defend the Muslims.

253
00:18:15,869 --> 00:18:19,847
The muslims, by the way also had battle cry in Khandaq(خندق) and that was,

254
00:18:19,927 --> 00:18:21,568
حم لا يُنْصَرُوْنْ

255
00:18:21,984 --> 00:18:24,928
They will not be victorious, they will not be victorious.

256
00:18:25,864 --> 00:18:27,239
The story of Hudaifah(حذيفة);

257
00:18:27,852 --> 00:18:33,759
And I'll read to you two narrations one is narration of Ahmed(احمد) and the other one is narration of Muslim(مسلم).

258
00:18:34,334 --> 00:18:37,711
 The narration of Ahmad(احمد) which is a bit more detailed.

259
00:18:38,447 --> 00:18:44,941
A man from Kufa(كوفه) asked  Hudaifah Bin Yamaan( حذيفة بن يمان) have you actually seen the Messenger of Allah

260
00:18:45,375 --> 00:18:47,351
and you were you really a companion of his.

261
00:18:47,416 --> 00:18:49,422
So this happened in the time of Taba'een(تابعين).

262
00:18:49,871 --> 00:18:51,948
Hudaifah(حذيفة) said, Oh, yes nephew.

263
00:18:52,487 --> 00:18:55,767
So, this Taba'e(تابعي) said, Then how did you get by?

264
00:18:56,195 --> 00:18:59,100
How did you treat him, how did you deal with him?

265
00:18:59,913 --> 00:19:05,344
Hudaifah(حذيفه) said, It was difficult for us, I swear by Allah, but we tried our best.

266
00:19:06,137 --> 00:19:08,139
So, this man, this Taba'e(تابعي) said;

267
00:19:08,265 --> 00:19:16,816
I swear if we'd lived at his time we'd never have let his foot, so much, as touch the ground.

268
00:19:17,296 --> 00:19:19,762
We'd have carried him on our shoulders.

269
00:19:20,532 --> 00:19:26,333
This Taba'e(تابعي) heard stories about how the Sahabah(صحابه) were with Rasool Allah ﷺ

270
00:19:26,673 --> 00:19:29,994
and he felt that if Rasool Allah ﷺ came in their time

271
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:32,883
they would have treated him much better than the Sahabah(صحابه).

272
00:19:33,403 --> 00:19:35,527
He said, we would have carried them on our shoulders

273
00:19:35,642 --> 00:19:38,487
we wouldn't even let his feet touch the ground.

274
00:19:39,686 --> 00:19:42,757
Now, Hudaifah(حذيفة) wants to teach this man a lesson

275
00:19:42,957 --> 00:19:47,219
and let him understand that, it's easier said, than done.

276
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:52,337
You know Yeah, now because we brought Islam to you, it is the Sahabah(صحابه) who brought to Taba'een(تابعين).

277
00:19:52,576 --> 00:19:54,618
And now because Islam was brought to you,

278
00:19:54,790 --> 00:19:59,210
and you understand how great Rasool Allah ﷺ is,

279
00:19:59,401 --> 00:20:03,795
and you see the fruits of his mission and you see the Khilafah(خِلَافَه), that he established.

280
00:20:04,341 --> 00:20:08,053
Now you say, Well, if we were living then, we would have done so and so.

281
00:20:09,146 --> 00:20:11,022
But this Taba'e(تابعي) doesn't understand that

282
00:20:11,567 --> 00:20:16,384
these were men, who were living with Rasool Allah ﷺ, and they had to fight their fathers,

283
00:20:16,429 --> 00:20:20,621
 they had to fight their brothers, they had to fight their clans, they had to give up their wealth

284
00:20:20,733 --> 00:20:22,936
they had to sacrifice their life, so it wasn't easy.

285
00:20:23,338 --> 00:20:27,371
Yeah, it's easy now to say that we would have carried Rasool Allah ﷺ on our shoulders.

286
00:20:27,777 --> 00:20:30,572
But if you were there you would have maybe act differently.

287
00:20:31,473 --> 00:20:36,097
So, Hudaifah(حذيفة) he wants to give him an example of how the situation was

288
00:20:36,615 --> 00:20:40,389
and how difficult it was, he's telling him about the reality.

289
00:20:40,429 --> 00:20:41,350
He said;

290
00:20:41,929 --> 00:20:46,930
Nephew, I swear, I see as now with the Messenger of Allah at Al-Khandaq(الخندق)

291
00:20:47,606 --> 00:20:51,969
and after he prayed for part of the night, he turned to us and asked.

292
00:20:52,632 --> 00:20:56,683
Who will volunteer to go and see what the enemy is doing and then come back.

293
00:20:57,476 --> 00:21:01,995
The Messenger of Allah stipulated, that if the volunteer would come back

294
00:21:02,409 --> 00:21:05,899
he would ask the Allah, that the man be his companion in paradise.

295
00:21:06,656 --> 00:21:12,998
But so severe was the fear, cold and hunger, that not one person volunteered.

296
00:21:13,869 --> 00:21:21,145
Rasool Allah ﷺ is asking for a volunteer, and this volunteer will be with him in Jannah(جنة),

297
00:21:21,589 --> 00:21:25,187
all what you have to do is go and visit the camp of the enemy and come back.

298
00:21:25,486 --> 00:21:28,792
Hudaifah(حذيفة) said, None of us stood up, none of us volunteered.

299
00:21:29,307 --> 00:21:33,576
Why? Because we were so terrified, it was cold, we were so hungry.

300
00:21:34,017 --> 00:21:36,750
And when you are in a situation like that, you can't think straight.

301
00:21:37,930 --> 00:21:39,229
So, none of us stood up.

302
00:21:39,881 --> 00:21:41,924
Rasool Allah ﷺ he then said;

303
00:21:42,151 --> 00:21:45,174
Since no one had risen he called upon me

304
00:21:45,679 --> 00:21:49,171
and once he had done so, I had no alternative, but to do so.

305
00:21:49,432 --> 00:21:52,982
So, now Rasool Allah ﷺ was not asking for volunteer, he said Hudaifah(حذيفة) you go.

306
00:21:53,776 --> 00:21:57,248
He then told me, Hudaifah(حذيفة) go and infiltrate the enemy

307
00:21:57,646 --> 00:21:59,400
go and see what they are doing,

308
00:21:59,725 --> 00:22:03,638
but don't cause any trouble, then returned to us.

309
00:22:04,338 --> 00:22:07,480
Hudaifah رضي الله عنه said, so I did.

310
00:22:08,162 --> 00:22:12,186
The Gale, an Allah's soldiers were greatly damaging them

311
00:22:12,524 --> 00:22:16,685
leaving them no fire, nor pots, nor tents, upright.

312
00:22:16,915 --> 00:22:20,225
The wind was so strong it was blowing everything.

313
00:22:20,487 --> 00:22:26,029
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) arose and said, Quraish(ابوسفيان) every man check out the person sitting next to him.

314
00:22:26,471 --> 00:22:32,079
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) was worried that in such a condition where the wind is blowing so fiercely

315
00:22:32,642 --> 00:22:36,244
the enemy could possibly try to infiltrate us.

316
00:22:36,647 --> 00:22:39,967
So, Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) said, that everyone check the person next to him.

317
00:22:40,708 --> 00:22:46,738
Hudaifah رضي الله عنه, he said, at this I took the hand of the man next to me and asked him, his name.

318
00:22:47,150 --> 00:22:52,904
So, Hudaifah(حذيفة) acted very quickly rather than have somebody asked him, he asked the man next to him.

319
00:22:53,833 --> 00:22:56,402
Very smart move, it saved him, his life.

320
00:22:56,869 --> 00:22:58,321
He told me, who he was.

321
00:22:58,639 --> 00:23:02,445
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) then said, We're not in a permanent camp.

322
00:23:02,884 --> 00:23:07,962
Our horses and camels are dying, and Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه), are at odds with us.

323
00:23:08,415 --> 00:23:11,450
And we've heard things about them that we don't like.

324
00:23:12,204 --> 00:23:14,606
You can see what we've lost, due to the Gale.

325
00:23:14,796 --> 00:23:17,230
How our cooking pots, won't stay upright.

326
00:23:17,790 --> 00:23:21,196
And we can't keep fires burning and our tents standing,

327
00:23:21,677 --> 00:23:24,240
you should leave, as I am about to do.

328
00:23:24,454 --> 00:23:26,067
That's it, they're giving up.

329
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:29,048
He then went to his camel, which was hobbled,

330
00:23:29,484 --> 00:23:35,675
mounted it, struck it so that it arose on three legs since he only on hobbled it, when it was standing.

331
00:23:36,165 --> 00:23:40,794
If it had not been for the promise that the messenger of Allah, made me

332
00:23:40,872 --> 00:23:42,961
make not to cause trouble

333
00:23:43,266 --> 00:23:44,863
I could have shot him, with an arrow.

334
00:23:44,935 --> 00:23:49,570
Because remember, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him don't cause any trouble just go gather information and come back.

335
00:23:50,559 --> 00:23:51,728
Hudaifah(حذيفة) went on.

336
00:23:52,070 --> 00:23:54,050
So, I returned to the Messenger of Allah

337
00:23:54,395 --> 00:23:59,118
and found him, standing in prayer shrouded in a wrap belonging to one of his wives.

338
00:23:59,482 --> 00:24:03,540
When he saw me, he asked me to come in, to sit, at his feet

339
00:24:03,682 --> 00:24:06,492
and threw an end of the wrap over me,

340
00:24:06,936 --> 00:24:09,659
he then bowed and prostrated, while I was under it

341
00:24:10,015 --> 00:24:13,308
when he was finished, I related the news to him.

342
00:24:13,961 --> 00:24:16,426
When Ghatafaan(غطفان) heard what Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) had done.

343
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:18,291
They hurried of home.

344
00:24:18,640 --> 00:24:19,847
So, now everybody left.

345
00:24:19,950 --> 00:24:21,116
This is the narration of Ahmad(احمد).

346
00:24:21,156 --> 00:24:27,403
The narration of Muslim(مسلم) is narrated from Yazeed At-Taymi(يزيد التيمي), from his father who said;

347
00:24:27,820 --> 00:24:30,528
We were with Hudaifah(حذيفة), when a man told him

348
00:24:30,893 --> 00:24:35,946
if I had been alive with the Messenger of Allah, I would have fought alongside him, heroically.

349
00:24:36,622 --> 00:24:38,681
So, Hudaifah(حذيفة) said: Would it you indeed?

350
00:24:39,078 --> 00:24:39,954
Is that the case?

351
00:24:40,062 --> 00:24:43,455
Now claiming that you would have fought fiercely with Rasool Allah ﷺ

352
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:46,114
and then Hudaifah(حذيفة) told him;

353
00:24:46,233 --> 00:24:50,368
Once we were there at the Battle of Al-Ahzaab(احزاب) with Rasool Allah ﷺ

354
00:24:50,566 --> 00:24:53,739
it was nighttime and there was a fierce cold Gale blowing.

355
00:24:54,057 --> 00:24:55,057
He asked us;

356
00:24:55,268 --> 00:25:00,085
Is there no man who will bring me the news of the enemy and be with me at judgment day.

357
00:25:00,593 --> 00:25:04,305
When none of us responded, he asked the same question a second and a third time.

358
00:25:04,929 --> 00:25:08,720
Then he said: "Hudaifah(حذيفة), you go and bring us, news of the enemy.

359
00:25:09,317 --> 00:25:13,440
Since he had called upon me by name, I had no alternative but to get up.

360
00:25:14,477 --> 00:25:19,679
He then said: "Bring me news of them, without giving them any cause for alarm about me."

361
00:25:20,372 --> 00:25:22,743
So, I left and made my way to them

362
00:25:23,255 --> 00:25:25,508
feeling as if I was walking through a public bath,

363
00:25:25,606 --> 00:25:29,704
meaning here public baths, it's talking about the heat, he was feeling hot.

364
00:25:30,216 --> 00:25:33,704
I found Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) there, warming his back to the fire

365
00:25:34,220 --> 00:25:38,398
I placed an arrow in the center of my bow and I was about to release it

366
00:25:38,471 --> 00:25:43,246
when I remembered how Rasool Allah ﷺ had told me, not to give them any alarm about it.

367
00:25:44,015 --> 00:25:46,662
If I had shot it, I would have hit him.

368
00:25:46,997 --> 00:25:52,818
I then left to return to Rasool Allah ﷺ and again the feeling of walking in a bath overcame me.

369
00:25:53,230 --> 00:25:56,708
 When I arrived back, I felt very cold and chilled once again.

370
00:25:57,097 --> 00:26:01,213
I told this to him and he put over me part of the cloak, he was wearing, as he prayed.

371
00:26:02,227 --> 00:26:04,819
He slept right on, through till morning

372
00:26:05,313 --> 00:26:08,490
when he spoke to me saying, up you get sleepy head.

373
00:26:09,312 --> 00:26:12,796
So, Hudaifah(حذيفة) here is telling this man that, Well, this was our situation.

374
00:26:12,858 --> 00:26:18,962
So, you need to ask yourself again, whether you would have fought alongside Rasool Allah ﷺ heroically.

375
00:26:19,677 --> 00:26:21,872
Now, you're saying that years later

376
00:26:22,535 --> 00:26:26,155
only Allah would know, what would happen if you were there at that difficult moment,

377
00:26:26,636 --> 00:26:29,671
whether you would have been with the Munafiqeen(منافقين) or with the Momineen(مؤمنين).

378
00:26:30,657 --> 00:26:33,675
So, we should try to avoid making all these big claims

379
00:26:33,715 --> 00:26:37,406
of what we can do and how we're going to give victory to Islam,

380
00:26:37,446 --> 00:26:39,358
Just do it, Don't talk about it, Do it.

381
00:26:39,983 --> 00:26:42,444
That's our problem today, everybody is proposing a solution,

382
00:26:42,484 --> 00:26:47,614
everybody's saying that I'm going to do this and do that for the religion and nothing gets done.

383
00:26:49,162 --> 00:26:54,115
Now, Ghatafaan(غطفان) and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they just left that's it.

384
00:26:54,566 --> 00:26:59,651
Rasool Allah ﷺ wakes up next day in the morning and takes a look at the empty campground.

385
00:27:00,071 --> 00:27:00,986
 No one is left.

386
00:27:01,701 --> 00:27:05,861
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and Ghatafaan(غطفان) have left, as if there was no Ahzaab(احزاب)

387
00:27:06,299 --> 00:27:07,869
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

388
00:27:08,522 --> 00:27:16,257
لا إله إلا الله وَحْدَه، صَدَقَ وَعْدَه، وَنَصَرَ عَبْدَه، وَهَزَمَ الْأَحْزَابَ وَحْدَهَ

389
00:27:16,472 --> 00:27:17,814
لا إله إلا الله

390
00:27:18,052 --> 00:27:21,171
There's no one worthy of worship except Allah

391
00:27:21,364 --> 00:27:22,549
صَدَقَ وَعْدَه

392
00:27:22,710 --> 00:27:24,129
His promise came true.

393
00:27:24,645 --> 00:27:25,820
 وَنَصَرَ عَبْدَه

394
00:27:26,058 --> 00:27:27,954
And he gave victory to His servant,

395
00:27:28,417 --> 00:27:30,275
وَهَزَمَ الْأَحْزَابَ وَحْدَهَ

396
00:27:30,550 --> 00:27:33,489
And He defeated the coalition alone.

397
00:27:33,997 --> 00:27:37,506
It was Allah, Who defeated the coalition and He did it alone.

398
00:27:38,334 --> 00:27:40,963
Miracles, we've been talking about miracles in the Ghazawat(غزوات)

399
00:27:41,037 --> 00:27:44,291
what are the miracles that happened in Ghazwat Al-Khandaq(غزوة الخندق).?

400
00:27:45,116 --> 00:27:47,638
When the Muslims were digging the trench

401
00:27:48,350 --> 00:27:51,660
Jabir Ibn Abdullah(جابربن عبدالله) saw the condition of Rasool Allah ﷺ

402
00:27:52,474 --> 00:27:57,256
People were tying one stone to their stomachs and he had two stones tied to his stomach.

403
00:27:58,272 --> 00:27:59,748
So, he goes back to his wife

404
00:28:00,321 --> 00:28:04,849
and he tells her, I've seen Rasool Allah ﷺ in an intolerable condition.

405
00:28:05,595 --> 00:28:06,917
Do you have any food for him?

406
00:28:07,420 --> 00:28:11,464
She said, All I have is some barley and a small goat.

407
00:28:12,418 --> 00:28:14,638
Jabir(جابر) goes and slaughters the goat.

408
00:28:15,059 --> 00:28:19,563
And he tells his wife to prepare some dough for baking bread.

409
00:28:20,158 --> 00:28:24,063
And while the meat was cooking, and she was baking the bread

410
00:28:24,553 --> 00:28:28,682
he goes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and tells him; I have some food for you.

411
00:28:29,722 --> 00:28:33,734
So, you can come along with one or two of your companions.

412
00:28:34,669 --> 00:28:36,839
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, and how much food should you have.?

413
00:28:36,894 --> 00:28:37,592
He told him,

414
00:28:37,886 --> 00:28:39,878
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, Oh, that's plenty.

415
00:28:40,895 --> 00:28:44,719
Tell your wife not to move the soup.

416
00:28:44,830 --> 00:28:46,108
The meat was cooked in soup,

417
00:28:46,148 --> 00:28:49,933
not to move the meat or soup, from its place, until I come.

418
00:28:50,616 --> 00:28:56,936
 And then Rasool Allah ﷺ stands up and to the amazement of Jabir(جابر), Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

419
00:28:57,040 --> 00:29:01,729
O Muhajiroon(مهاجرون), O Ansaar(انصار), Jabir(جابر) has prepared some food for you.

420
00:29:02,652 --> 00:29:06,403
Jabir(جابر) has told Rasool Allah ﷺ, to come along with one or two

421
00:29:07,105 --> 00:29:10,078
and Rasool Allah has invited the entire camp.

422
00:29:10,555 --> 00:29:12,530
All of you are invited to Jabir(جابر)'s house.

423
00:29:12,612 --> 00:29:15,890
Jabir(جابر) runs back home very embarrassed.

424
00:29:16,842 --> 00:29:18,954
What in the world are we going to do?

425
00:29:18,994 --> 00:29:22,184
 And you know, when you invite people and there's not enough food that's very embarrassing.

426
00:29:22,782 --> 00:29:24,392
He goes to his wife tells her

427
00:29:24,966 --> 00:29:27,611
you know what Rasool Allah is coming along with all of Ahl-Al-Khandaq(اهل الخندق)

428
00:29:27,660 --> 00:29:29,504
everyone is coming, He was worried.

429
00:29:29,587 --> 00:29:30,335
So she said;

430
00:29:30,555 --> 00:29:32,007
Did he ask you, how much food we have?

431
00:29:32,087 --> 00:29:32,798
He said, Yes.

432
00:29:33,302 --> 00:29:34,887
And he told him, he said, Yes

433
00:29:35,334 --> 00:29:38,167
She said, Allah and His Messenger know best.

434
00:29:38,389 --> 00:29:40,596
Jabir(جابر) said those words comforted me.

435
00:29:41,923 --> 00:29:44,199
He knows best, you already told him, how much food we have.

436
00:29:44,691 --> 00:29:49,832
Rasool Allah comes in, and he would pour the soup and the meat

437
00:29:50,112 --> 00:29:51,908
and then he would crush bread over it.

438
00:29:52,028 --> 00:29:53,410
So, he was doing the dishing.

439
00:29:54,084 --> 00:29:57,705
And he told the Sahabah(صحابه) to come in and not crowd each other

440
00:29:58,667 --> 00:29:59,987
come in, in groups,

441
00:30:00,399 --> 00:30:02,994
 because they were very hungry you could have a stampede.

442
00:30:03,497 --> 00:30:07,022
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them slow down, come in, in groups.

443
00:30:08,001 --> 00:30:10,032
They would come in groups of 10

444
00:30:10,649 --> 00:30:14,023
Rasool Allah would prepare the food for them and bring it to them

445
00:30:14,520 --> 00:30:17,633
They would eat and then they would leave, another 10 would come in

446
00:30:17,954 --> 00:30:22,054
Rasool Allah ﷺ would prepare the meal for them, and so on and so forth.

447
00:30:22,876 --> 00:30:28,233
In one narration it says that 800 people ate from that meal.

448
00:30:29,115 --> 00:30:33,813
And when they were done, Rasool Allah ﷺ went back and the pot was full as it was,

449
00:30:34,083 --> 00:30:37,291
and the bread was still baking in the oven.

450
00:30:37,809 --> 00:30:41,743
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told the wife of Jabir(جابر) to feed her neighbors.

451
00:30:42,758 --> 00:30:46,527
This was a miracle of Rasool Allah ﷺ, increasing the food.

452
00:30:46,693 --> 00:30:47,823
 كَثِيْرُ الطَّعَامْ

453
00:30:49,008 --> 00:30:53,372
Another miracle, when they were digging the trench,

454
00:30:54,372 --> 00:30:59,263
a boulder stood in their way and they couldn't move it or break it,

455
00:30:59,542 --> 00:31:01,983
in fact it was breaking their axes.

456
00:31:02,399 --> 00:31:04,776
So they came to Rasool Allahﷺ and told him about it.

457
00:31:05,089 --> 00:31:07,449
Rasool Ullah went there, grabbed an axe

458
00:31:07,845 --> 00:31:10,329
 and said, Bismillah(بسم الله) and struck it.

459
00:31:11,274 --> 00:31:14,843
A lightening came out and Rasool Allah ﷺ said Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر).

460
00:31:15,910 --> 00:31:20,260
He struck it again, light came out and he said Allah O Akbar(الله اكبر),

461
00:31:20,962 --> 00:31:24,255
he struck it a third time and then it disintegrated into dust

462
00:31:24,342 --> 00:31:25,848
 and Rasool Ullah said, Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر)

463
00:31:26,870 --> 00:31:29,887
So, Salman(سلمان) asked him, O Messenger of Allah Why were you saying Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر)?

464
00:31:29,973 --> 00:31:33,871
And what was that light coming out like, lightning from this Boulder?

465
00:31:34,417 --> 00:31:37,356
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, the first time I struck it.

466
00:31:38,561 --> 00:31:47,034
I was given the glad tidings of opening, of conquering the Roman Empire,

467
00:31:47,717 --> 00:31:52,590
and I could see the red palaces of Syria from right here.

468
00:31:53,502 --> 00:31:55,480
The second time I said, Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر)

469
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:59,079
I was given the glad tidings of conquering the Persian Empire

470
00:31:59,611 --> 00:32:02,897
and I was able to see it's white palace from right here.

471
00:32:03,388 --> 00:32:05,746
And the third time I said, Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر) is that

472
00:32:06,108 --> 00:32:08,714
I was given the glad tidings of conquering Yemen

473
00:32:09,249 --> 00:32:12,181
and I was able to see the gates of San'a(صنعا) from right here.

474
00:32:13,610 --> 00:32:18,947
Now, notice here that Rasool Allah ﷺ is giving them these glad tidings in the worst of times,

475
00:32:19,635 --> 00:32:24,627
when the morale was low, when you look around you and what you see is defeat

476
00:32:25,097 --> 00:32:26,673
when you are besieged.

477
00:32:27,768 --> 00:32:30,078
But that's the whole point of giving a glad tidings.

478
00:32:31,395 --> 00:32:33,886
That is, when glad tidings should be given.

479
00:32:34,569 --> 00:32:37,289
It is when you were weak when you're almost going to give up.

480
00:32:37,942 --> 00:32:42,269
So now if the Ummah(امة) is weak, divided, defeated

481
00:32:43,404 --> 00:32:46,857
we should give the glad tidings that Rasool Allah ﷺ has given us

482
00:32:47,875 --> 00:32:50,246
سَيَبْلُغُ هَذَا الدِّيْنَ ما بَلَغَ اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارْ،

483
00:32:50,669 --> 00:32:54,192
This religion will reach as far as night and day can reach.

484
00:32:54,751 --> 00:32:59,055
إنّ الله زَوَى لِيَ الْأَرْضْ فَرَأَيْتَ اَن مُلْكَ اُمَّتِيْ سَيَبْلُغُ مَا زُويَّ لِيْ مِنْهَا

485
00:32:59,360 --> 00:33:01,076
Allah has shown me the entire earth

486
00:33:01,116 --> 00:33:03,985
 and he told me that the kingdom of my nation will reach all of it.

487
00:33:05,403 --> 00:33:08,675
So, victory belongs to this Ummah(امة), and it's coming.

488
00:33:09,564 --> 00:33:14,477
The third miracle Rasool Allah ﷺ saw Ammar Bin Yasir(عمار بن ياسر) working hard.

489
00:33:14,613 --> 00:33:15,278
And he told him;

490
00:33:15,318 --> 00:33:18,390
 يَا عَمَّارْ،تَقْتُلُكَ الْفِئَتُ الْبَاغِيَّهْ

491
00:33:18,709 --> 00:33:23,748
Ya Ammar(عَمَّار), you will be killed by the aggressing party.

492
00:33:24,666 --> 00:33:25,294
That's up.

493
00:33:25,659 --> 00:33:27,683
You will be killed by the aggressing party.

494
00:33:27,954 --> 00:33:30,270
Ammar(عَمَّار) lives through the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

495
00:33:30,310 --> 00:33:33,846
lives through the era of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), Umar(عمر), Uthman(عثمان).

496
00:33:34,529 --> 00:33:37,783
And then in the time of Ali(علي), he joins in the army of Ali(علي)

497
00:33:38,089 --> 00:33:41,534
and was killed by the army of Muawiya(معاويه).

498
00:33:42,581 --> 00:33:47,652
So, this Hadith(حديث) tells us that the party of Ali(علي) was right,

499
00:33:48,018 --> 00:33:50,859
while the party of Muawiya(معاويه) was wrong.

500
00:33:51,328 --> 00:33:57,320
And this was news of Al-Ghaib(الغيب) that Rasool Allah ﷺ was given by Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

501
00:33:57,599 --> 00:34:02,809
And he was told that Ammar(عَمَّار) will be killed by the aggressive party.

502
00:34:02,864 --> 00:34:04,817
Now both of them are Muslim parties.

503
00:34:05,682 --> 00:34:10,400
But one of them was right and one of them was wrong.

504
00:34:11,916 --> 00:34:16,682
Let's just talk briefly about lessons from the story of Hudaifah(حذيفة) which we just mentioned.

505
00:34:17,373 --> 00:34:20,840
First of all, the discipline is very important for the Muslim

506
00:34:21,749 --> 00:34:26,092
who is working in a Jama'ah(جماعة), to have discipline.

507
00:34:27,306 --> 00:34:30,344
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, Don't cause any trouble.

508
00:34:31,076 --> 00:34:34,900
So, Hudaifah(حذيفة) even though, he had Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) in his sights

509
00:34:34,980 --> 00:34:36,682
 and he could have shot him and killed him.

510
00:34:37,264 --> 00:34:42,470
He stopped because of the order of Rasool Allah ﷺ, that is discipline.

511
00:34:44,034 --> 00:34:49,482
Now number two, he didn't feel cold throughout this journey.

512
00:34:49,896 --> 00:34:51,043
 And that's a Karamah(كرامة).

513
00:34:51,781 --> 00:34:53,723
Number three, his fast response.

514
00:34:54,555 --> 00:34:58,610
As soon as Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) said that everyone check out the man next to him.

515
00:34:59,073 --> 00:35:01,844
Hudaifah(حذيفة) was the one, who took the initiative and did that.

516
00:35:02,719 --> 00:35:06,117
And finally between theory and reality

517
00:35:06,495 --> 00:35:09,903
you know, that Taba'ee(التابعي) was talking about theory,

518
00:35:10,322 --> 00:35:12,630
while Hudaifah(حذيفة) was talking about reality

519
00:35:12,735 --> 00:35:14,416
and there's a difference between the two.

520
00:35:14,741 --> 00:35:18,060
So don't assume things, until they happen

521
00:35:18,750 --> 00:35:25,376
and don't have too much confidence in yourself and in your Eeman(ايمان), until you are tested

522
00:35:25,719 --> 00:35:30,600
 because one cannot know the results, until after the exam is given.

523
00:35:32,132 --> 00:35:34,896
Some lessons from Ghazwa Al-Khandaq(غزوة الخندق).

524
00:35:35,216 --> 00:35:42,596
Number one, for the Jews to ally themselves with the Mushrikeen(مشركين) against the Muslims is contradictory.

525
00:35:43,397 --> 00:35:46,957
You know, why would they ally themselves with the Mushrikeen(مشركين)?

526
00:35:47,276 --> 00:35:51,157
When they are closer, in terms of similarity of religion to the Muslims,

527
00:35:52,277 --> 00:35:55,652
but even though it is contradicting we shouldn't be surprised

528
00:35:56,533 --> 00:36:00,726
and that is still repeating, until this day.

529
00:36:01,829 --> 00:36:10,585
Contradicting theories, or political views will come together to fight the religion of truth.

530
00:36:11,312 --> 00:36:18,471
Can't you see today that the West, the Democratic West, the West of the human rights,

531
00:36:18,971 --> 00:36:24,362
 the West that claims to be fighting for the sake of spreading democracy

532
00:36:25,076 --> 00:36:31,411
is aligning itself with the most autocratic and oppressive regimes on the face of the earth.

533
00:36:32,007 --> 00:36:33,221
 For the sake of what?

534
00:36:33,665 --> 00:36:35,276
For the sake of fighting Islam.

535
00:36:36,248 --> 00:36:38,883
So, one shouldn't be surprised, it's number one.

536
00:36:39,464 --> 00:36:43,150
Number two, make use of the available technology

537
00:36:43,370 --> 00:36:46,590
a Muslim should make use of available technology.

538
00:36:47,446 --> 00:36:51,119
Rasool Allah ﷺ approved the idea of Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي)

539
00:36:51,951 --> 00:36:56,977
bringing in a foreign idea an idea that belonged to the Kuffar(كفار) it belong to the Persians

540
00:36:58,370 --> 00:37:02,893
but since it is not, in an issue of religion, it's a matter of strategy

541
00:37:03,227 --> 00:37:07,337
Rasool Allah ﷺ adopted that idea, which was novel to Arab warfare.

542
00:37:08,542 --> 00:37:09,520
Number three,

543
00:37:10,172 --> 00:37:13,174
 the example of leadership, given by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

544
00:37:13,589 --> 00:37:15,433
He was digging the trench with them

545
00:37:15,868 --> 00:37:24,519
not for the sake of bringing the TV cameras to show the leader as part of the people and make a big political propaganda out of it.

546
00:37:24,577 --> 00:37:27,470
No, Rasool Allah ﷺ was doing it, Sincerely.

547
00:37:28,098 --> 00:37:31,848
And to give us the example of how a leader should act.

548
00:37:32,863 --> 00:37:34,625
He goes hungry like they did.

549
00:37:35,591 --> 00:37:39,399
And when he finds food, he shares it with them.

550
00:37:39,672 --> 00:37:46,188
He didn't just invite the one and two, that Jabir(جابر) said but he invited the whole camp, to go and feed with him.

551
00:37:47,366 --> 00:37:50,884
Next lesson, He was raising the morale through Nasheed(نشيد).

552
00:37:51,611 --> 00:37:56,520
They were chanting those words of poetry, to raise up the spirit.

553
00:37:57,041 --> 00:38:00,201
So, the leader should have the highest spirit among the group,

554
00:38:00,440 --> 00:38:07,670
because he is the person whom the followers, take refuge in when things get tough.

555
00:38:08,087 --> 00:38:13,209
So, if they find that the leader is weak and the leader has already given up, they'll do the same.

556
00:38:14,573 --> 00:38:15,407
The next lesson,

557
00:38:15,926 --> 00:38:19,625
The reaction of Rasool Allah ﷺ to the news of Quraidha's(قريظه) treachery

558
00:38:19,690 --> 00:38:23,765
we talked about when he sent out Sa'ad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ), Sa'ad Bin Ubadah(سعد بن عبادة),

559
00:38:23,805 --> 00:38:25,350
 and Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة)

560
00:38:25,674 --> 00:38:31,228
to go and check out if Quraidha's(قريظه) have broken their agreement with Rasool Allah ﷺ

561
00:38:31,774 --> 00:38:38,090
and he told them, If you find that, to be the case then hinted to me without letting the people know,

562
00:38:38,306 --> 00:38:39,807
 don't weaken their morale.

563
00:38:40,341 --> 00:38:44,965
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ when the news was delivered to him

564
00:38:45,615 --> 00:38:46,819
he said Abshiro'oo(ابشرو).

565
00:38:47,338 --> 00:38:49,755
He said, receive the glad tidings.

566
00:38:49,795 --> 00:38:51,297
So Rasool Ullah was optimistic,

567
00:38:52,105 --> 00:38:57,148
even though at that moment and this would give confidence to the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

568
00:38:57,827 --> 00:39:04,913
And finally, difficult times show what is in the hearts of men.

569
00:39:05,274 --> 00:39:06,486
Ibn Is'haq(ابن اسحاق) said;

570
00:39:07,125 --> 00:39:09,505
when conditions worsened, he was talking about Al-Khandaq(الخندق),

571
00:39:09,545 --> 00:39:17,339
when conditions worsened, so did the attitude of many people and they began saying, ugly things.

572
00:39:17,719 --> 00:39:21,235
So the attitude changed, under the stress.

573
00:39:21,884 --> 00:39:24,431
And they started saying, ugly things

574
00:39:24,471 --> 00:39:27,850
in terms of ugly things in Aqeedah(عقيدة), ugly things about Islam

575
00:39:28,433 --> 00:39:33,594
ugly things that show weakness in the personality, weakness in the trust in Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

576
00:39:34,688 --> 00:39:38,707
So, one needs to prepare themselves for difficult situations,

577
00:39:39,343 --> 00:39:42,831
don't go by your conduct in terms of ease,

578
00:39:43,250 --> 00:39:45,957
but you need to prepare yourselves for times of difficulty,

579
00:39:46,891 --> 00:39:49,031
because that is when, the truth comes out.

580
00:39:49,984 --> 00:39:54,654
We talked about the Munafiqeen(منافقين), and we recited the Ayat(آيات) relating to the Munafiqeen(منافقين).

581
00:39:54,921 --> 00:39:58,301
What about the Mumineen(مؤمنين), what about the believers?

582
00:39:59,250 --> 00:40:03,098
What did Allah say about them, regarding in the context of Al-Ahzaab(الاحزاب)?

583
00:40:04,078 --> 00:40:08,066
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says, and these Ayaat(آيات) are in Surat Ul Ahzaab(سورة الاحزاب)

584
00:40:08,344 --> 00:40:13,254
which is Surah(سورة) named after the coalition, Al-Ahzaab(الاحزاب) Allahعَزّوجَلّ said;

585
00:40:13,781 --> 00:40:20,361
لَقَدْ كَانَ لَكُمْ فِي رَسُولِ اللَّهِ أُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌلِمَنْ

586
00:40:20,705 --> 00:40:28,613
لِمَنْ كَانَ يَرْجُو اللَّهَ وَالْيَوْمَ الْآخِرَ وَذَكَرَ اللَّهَ كَثِيرًا۝

587
00:40:29,584 --> 00:40:38,634
وَلَمَّا رَأَى الْمُؤْمِنُونَ الْأَحْزَابَ قَالُوا هَٰذَا مَا وَعَدَنَا اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ

588
00:40:39,045 --> 00:40:41,905
وَصَدَقَ اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ ۚ

589
00:40:42,136 --> 00:40:48,773
وَمَا زَادَهُمْ إِلَّا إِيمَانًا وَتَسْلِيمًاَ۝

590
00:40:49,065 --> 00:40:56,494
مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ رِجَالٌ صَدَقُوا مَا عَاهَدُوا اللَّهَ عَلَيْهِ

591
00:40:57,013 --> 00:41:03,969
فَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ قَضَىٰ نَحْبَهُ وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يَنْتَظِرُ

592
00:41:04,313 --> 00:41:07,758
وَمَا بَدَّلُوا تَبْدِيلاً۝

593
00:41:08,121 --> 00:41:14,531
There has certainly been for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent pattern, for anyone

594
00:41:14,986 --> 00:41:19,027
 whose hope is Allah and the last day and who remembers Allah often.

595
00:41:20,173 --> 00:41:22,575
And when the believers saw the companies, they said;

596
00:41:22,757 --> 00:41:26,378
This is what Allah and His Messenger had promised us

597
00:41:26,872 --> 00:41:29,165
and Allah and His messengers spoke the truth.

598
00:41:29,836 --> 00:41:32,941
And it increased them only in faith, and acceptance.

599
00:41:33,871 --> 00:41:37,661
Among the believers are men, true to what they promised Allah,

600
00:41:39,060 --> 00:41:43,852
among them is, he who has fulfilled his vows to death

601
00:41:44,507 --> 00:41:47,251
and among them is, he, who awaits his chance.

602
00:41:47,868 --> 00:41:51,715
And they did not alter the terms of their commitment by any alteration.

603
00:41:52,954 --> 00:41:59,249
There are certainly being for you and the Messenger of Allah an excellent pattern for anyone whose hope is Allah

604
00:41:59,587 --> 00:42:02,354
and the Last Day and remembers Allah often.

605
00:42:03,145 --> 00:42:05,649
This Ayah(آية), What was the context of it?

606
00:42:05,915 --> 00:42:07,561
See, this is Ayah(آية) is saying,

607
00:42:08,203 --> 00:42:11,289
 لَقَدْ كَانَ لَكُمْ فِي رَسُولِ اللَّهِ أُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ

608
00:42:12,185 --> 00:42:19,280
You have a good pattern of conduct in Rasool Allah ﷺ for you to emulate, for you to imitate in your life.

609
00:42:19,411 --> 00:42:21,733
So, this is Ayah(آية) is asking us, to follow the Sunnah(سنة)

610
00:42:22,341 --> 00:42:25,009
this is the Aayah(آية) in Qur'an that tells us to follow the Sunnah(سنة)

611
00:42:25,511 --> 00:42:27,752
we have an example in Rasool Allah follow it.

612
00:42:28,290 --> 00:42:34,438
Now was this Ayah(آية) revealed because one of the Muslims did not use the Maswaak(مسواك)?

613
00:42:35,583 --> 00:42:40,056
Was this Ayah(آية) reveal because one of the Muslims did not have their soab(ثوب) above the ankle?

614
00:42:40,962 --> 00:42:46,040
Was this Ayah(آية) revealed because one of the Muslims, did not grow a beard?

615
00:42:46,734 --> 00:42:48,637
All of this is part of Sunnah(سنة).

616
00:42:49,073 --> 00:42:51,636
But was this the reason why the Ayah(آية) was revealed?

617
00:42:52,887 --> 00:42:56,899
The reason why the Ayah(آية) was revealed according to Ibn Jarir At-Tabri(ابن جريرالطبري) is,

618
00:42:57,339 --> 00:43:01,891
Allah was reprimanding the believers, who stayed behind

619
00:43:02,457 --> 00:43:07,251
and didn't go and joined the camp, that was right next to the trench.

620
00:43:07,789 --> 00:43:09,228
So, Allah was telling them

621
00:43:09,740 --> 00:43:13,713
you should follow the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and go and be with him.

622
00:43:14,590 --> 00:43:17,538
And Ibn Abi Hatim(إبن ابي حاتم) narrates that As-Suddi(الثدي) said,

623
00:43:17,581 --> 00:43:21,570
As-Suddi(الثدي) one of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) said that it means here.

624
00:43:21,610 --> 00:43:22,977
 مُعَاسَافِ الْقِتَالْ

625
00:43:23,002 --> 00:43:26,924
You should be standing next to him in fighting, in Qitaal(قتال).

626
00:43:27,533 --> 00:43:30,853
This was the context in which the Ayah(آية) was revealed.

627
00:43:31,537 --> 00:43:34,591
So, nowadays it's unfortunate to hear people talk about Sunnah(سنة)

628
00:43:34,641 --> 00:43:37,754
but they completely neglect the issue of Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

629
00:43:37,981 --> 00:43:40,020
as being part of the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

630
00:43:40,560 --> 00:43:44,182
We should not overemphasize some parts of Sunnah(سنة) and neglect others.

631
00:43:44,526 --> 00:43:46,848
Sunnah(سنة) should be taken as a whole package.

632
00:43:47,916 --> 00:43:50,632
And then we prioritize among the Sunnah(سنة)

633
00:43:50,712 --> 00:43:55,824
 so we say all is important but some is more important than others.

634
00:43:56,146 --> 00:44:01,838
And since the Ayah(آية) was revealed in this context, definitely, this will be the most important Sunnah(سنة) of all.

635
00:44:03,231 --> 00:44:03,958
The next Ayah(آية);

636
00:44:03,998 --> 00:44:06,309
And when the believers saw the companies they said,

637
00:44:06,358 --> 00:44:08,482
This is what Allah and His messenger had promised us.

638
00:44:08,963 --> 00:44:12,129
See the Munafiqeen(منافقين), when they saw the coalition.

639
00:44:12,518 --> 00:44:13,518
They said;

640
00:44:13,733 --> 00:44:15,693
Allah has lied to us, Rasool Ullah has lied to us

641
00:44:15,733 --> 00:44:19,266
he's telling us that we're going to conquer the Persian Empire and the Roman Empire,

642
00:44:19,306 --> 00:44:21,158
we can't even feel safe going to the toilet.

643
00:44:21,508 --> 00:44:23,683
So, they were having doubts in the promise of Allah.

644
00:44:24,248 --> 00:44:26,366
What was the reaction of the believers?

645
00:44:26,406 --> 00:44:29,031
They said; This is exactly what Allah and His Messenger promised us,

646
00:44:29,071 --> 00:44:29,832
what does this mean?

647
00:44:30,399 --> 00:44:31,932
Allah says in Surat Ul Bakarah(سورة البقره)

648
00:44:32,393 --> 00:44:42,811
أَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ أَنْ تَدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَأْتِكُمْ مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ خَلَوْا مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ

649
00:44:43,310 --> 00:44:50,491
مَسَّتْهُمُ الْبَأْسَاءُ وَالضَّرَّاءُ وَزُلْزِلُوا

650
00:44:50,952 --> 00:44:59,694
 وَزُلْزِلُوا حَتَّىٰ يَقُولَ الرَّسُولُ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَعَهُ مَتَىٰ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ

651
00:45:00,141 --> 00:45:06,289
أَلَا إِنَّ نَصْرَ اللَّهِ قَرِيبٌ۝

652
00:45:06,588 --> 00:45:08,647
Do you think that you will enter into paradise

653
00:45:09,049 --> 00:45:12,254
without going through what the nations before you went through?

654
00:45:12,917 --> 00:45:16,928
They were tested by fear and hunger, by difficulty

655
00:45:17,624 --> 00:45:19,666
until they and the messenger said;

656
00:45:19,861 --> 00:45:23,053
When will we receive the victory of Allah?

657
00:45:23,264 --> 00:45:26,944
So it test them to the limit, until they start asking O Allah

658
00:45:27,272 --> 00:45:28,757
when are you going to give us victory.

659
00:45:29,825 --> 00:45:32,573
 So they said, This is what Allah promised us.

660
00:45:33,072 --> 00:45:35,580
Allah spoke about this in Surat Ul Bakarah(سورة البقره) and here it's happening

661
00:45:36,056 --> 00:45:37,951
it's happening just as we were promised.

662
00:45:38,482 --> 00:45:40,587
So it's only added to their Eeman(ايمان)

663
00:45:41,541 --> 00:45:44,732
because they saw the promise of Allah being fulfilled in front of their eyes.

664
00:45:44,868 --> 00:45:49,632
So you can see how the same event brought forth different reaction from the believers

665
00:45:49,690 --> 00:45:52,136
  and a different reaction from the Munafiqoon(منافقون)

666
00:45:52,338 --> 00:45:55,310
 and it increased them only in faith and acceptance.

667
00:45:56,611 --> 00:46:00,193
So, this was the reaction of Al-Muminoon(المؤمنون).

668
00:46:00,901 --> 00:46:05,631
In sha Allah ho Ta'ala(اِنْشَاءالله تعالى), tomorrow we'll talk about  Ghazwat Bannu Quraidha(غزوة بنوقريظه)

669
00:46:05,671 --> 00:46:12,467
 and that should be our final talk in this series of lectures on the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

670
00:46:12,979 --> 00:46:17,098
أَقُوْلُ قَوْلِي هَذَا وَأسْتَغْفِرُ اللهِ الْعَظِيْمْ وَلِيْ وَلَكُمْ فَاسْتَغْفِرُوْہ اِنَّه’غَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمْ

671
00:46:17,448 --> 00:46:20,733
وصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

672
00:46:21,094 --> 00:46:23,297
والسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاتهَ

